*.log
*.err
*.out
*.stdout.log
*.stderr.log
logs/
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
*.hprof
*.jfr
*.pid
*.lock
*.sock
*.exit

# --- Test trees -------------------------------------------------------------
# Developer material. CI runs hygiene and lint only; see the note at the top of
# .github/workflows/hygiene.yml before adding a test job.
tests/
test/
**/tests/
**/test/
test_*.py
*_test.py
*Test.java
*Tests.java
test-results/
test-results-*/
pytest-report*/
junit*.xml

# --- Model and training output ----------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.pkl
*.npz
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
checkpoints/
wandb/
mlruns/
tensorboard/

# --- Machine-written capture and report trees -------------------------------
# Large, regenerable, and in some cases containing a full server install.
/artifacts/
# Captured worlds and everything derived from them: Region snapshots, traversal
# navigation graphs and their manifests. ALL OR NOTHING on purpose -- the
# manifests attest to graph files by hash, so publishing a manifest without its
# graphs would describe a library that is not there. `hytalegym.jax.world.tokens`
# treats the whole set as absent and says so in the contract, which is what lets
# a clone without it still import.
HytaleRL/artifacts/
/output/
agents/ppo/artifacts/
agents/basic/artifacts/
arena/training/artifacts/
adk/runs/
adk/artifacts/
experimental/worldgen-v2/evidence/
experimental/*/evidence/
experimental/*/*/audits/
experimental/*/*/*/audits/

# --- Reverse-engineered server sources --------------------------------------
# Local reference material only. See LICENSE: these are not covered by it and
# are never distributed. CI fails the build if any are committed.
decompiled/
**/decompiled/
decompile/
**/decompile/
decomp/
**/decomp/

# --- Contributor documentation ----------------------------------------------
# Documents about doing the work rather than about the system. Anything
# user-facing should be a README.md instead, which publishes by default.
#
# `/docs/` is ANCHORED on purpose. A bare `docs/` matches at every depth and
# would swallow nested documentation directories that must publish, which is
# exactly the failure `tools/check_publication_hygiene.py` exists to catch.
DEV.md
**/DEV.md
DESIGN.md
**/DESIGN.md
MIGRATION.md
**/MIGRATION.md
AUDIT-*.md
**/AUDIT-*.md
CAPTURE-VS-*.md
**/CAPTURE-VS-*.md
SKILL.md
**/SKILL.md
STATUS.md
**/STATUS.md
/docs/
HytaleRL/docs/
experimental/worldgen-v2/documentation/

# --- Agent and session tooling ----------------------------------------------
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
skills/
**/skills/
*AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS*.md

# --- Generated session telemetry --------------------------------------------
!/telemetry/
/telemetry/*
!/telemetry/README.md
/telemetry/*.jsonl
/telemetry/*.jsonl.gz

# --- External mod configuration ---------------------------------------------
# Nothing in the published packages reads it.
/mods/

# --- Experimental trees with no published consumer --------------------------
# None are in `[tool.setuptools.packages.find]` or the ruff lint list, so none
# are part of the shipped product.
/experimental/3d_audio/
/experimental/hierarchical_planner/

# --- Hytale server runtime state ---------------------------------------------
# The server writes these at the repository root on first boot. They are
# operator state for one install, and a published default would be silently
# adopted by anyone who cloned it.
/bans.json
/whitelist.json
/permissions.json
/config.json

# The plugin keeps the same local state below its own install root.
HytaleRL/hytale-plugin/*.json
HytaleRL/hytale-plugin/telemetry/
HytaleRL/hytale-plugin/mods/

# --- Real source rescued from the rules above ------------------------------
# `**/skills/` targets agent skill folders, but `arena/training/skills/` is
# training source: `arena/training/__init__.py` imports it, so excluding it
# makes `import arena.training` fail on a fresh clone.
!arena/training/skills/

# `adk/runs/` is a run-artifact directory, but its `__init__.py` is the Run
# logging module that `adk/tools/run_minigame.py` imports. Keep the module,
# drop the run output.
!adk/runs/
adk/runs/*
!adk/runs/__init__.py

# --- Console storage root ---------------------------------------------------
# `console/core/storage.py` consolidates every console-written artifact under
# one root with named areas. It is entirely generated: runs, minted policies,
# captured worlds, logs, check results, dispatch scratch and native server
# state. None of it is source.
/storage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contributor-only material: handoffs, changelogs, issue registers, internal
# audits, one-off tools and probe dumps. None of it is user documentation --
# the README in each package is the public orientation layer instead.
#
# LISTED EXPLICITLY, NOT GLOBBED. `adk/docs/` and `console/docs/` also hold
# published files, so a directory rule here would take the README and the API
# reference with it.
#
# These paths were protected only by this machine's .git/info/exclude until CI
# caught it. That file never leaves the machine, so a fresh clone had no rule
# at all and `git add -A` there would have published every one of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
